<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for Amethyst and all of its helpers (main, renderer, GPU,
  plugin and the runtime utility process). Keep this list minimal; every addition weakens the
  hardened runtime and needs a reason here.

  com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit
    V8 (in every Electron process) and WebAssembly compile JavaScript to machine code at run
    time. On Apple Silicon that needs MAP_JIT pages, which the hardened runtime only permits
    with this entitlement. Without it every Electron process crashes at startup.

  Deliberately NOT included:
  - allow-unsigned-executable-memory: only needed by Electron < 12; MAP_JIT covers V8 today.
  - disable-library-validation: every framework and helper in the bundle is signed with our
    own Developer ID, and we load no third-party native modules. Java and Minecraft run as
    separate processes with their own signatures, so they are unaffected by our hardened
    runtime. Add this only if a future native module (e.g. a prebuilt .node signed by someone
    else) requires it.
  - allow-dyld-environment-variables, debugger, device/camera/audio access: not used.
  - com.apple.security.network.client: only meaningful inside the App Sandbox, which a
    Developer ID launcher that spawns Java does not use.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
  </dict>
</plist>
